# Cloudflare Pages redirects (also honored by Netlify during migration).
# Top-down order: first match wins, so SPA fallback must be LAST.
# Different-host redirects (mxqr.netlify.app → musixquare.com) live only
# in netlify.toml since Cloudflare won't see that hostname's traffic.
#
# Cloudflare Pages auto-handles directory index and `.html` stripping
# (e.g. `/landing` → `/landing.html`, `/designsystem` →
# `/designsystem/index.html`), so explicit wrapper rules aren't needed
# here. Adding them tripped Cloudflare's cycle-detection guard since
# `/foo → /foo/index.html` paired with the SPA catch-all looks like a
# strip-then-rematch loop. Netlify still has the same wrappers in
# netlify.toml; harmless duplication during migration.

# ── Case-variant redirects → canonical lowercase (301) ──
/DESIGNSYSTEM    /designsystem/    301
/DESIGNSYSTEM/   /designsystem/    301
/DesignSystem    /designsystem/    301
/DesignSystem/   /designsystem/    301
/CHANGELOG       /changelog/       301
/CHANGELOG/      /changelog/       301
/Changelog       /changelog/       301
/Changelog/      /changelog/       301
/ROADMAP         /roadmap/         301
/ROADMAP/        /roadmap/         301
/Roadmap         /roadmap/         301
/Roadmap/        /roadmap/         301

# ── SPA fallback ── must be the last rule
/*    /index.html    200
